THIRD-PARTY MATERIAL

The MIT grant above covers everything in this repository that the copyright
holders own: source, configuration, tooling, documentation, and the synthetic
corpus generated by this project.

It cannot and does not cover material owned by someone else, which keeps its own
terms. This is a statement of fact rather than a reservation — a licence can only
grant what the grantor holds. Two cases arise in practice:

  * Real-world artefacts ingested into the corpus under docs/DATASETS.md §6 are
    retained only with their own licence and provenance recorded per item, and
    items whose terms forbid redistribution are excluded from any release.

  * Model checkpoints under ml/artifacts/ are fine-tuned from third-party base
    models and inherit their obligations. MuRIL is Apache-2.0, which requires
    attribution and a NOTICE. Check the manifest recorded by
    ml/evaluation/manifest.py before redistributing a checkpoint.
